  <div class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This page describes how the Parking Lot app handles data. Last updated: March 2026.</p>

    <h2>What we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On your device:</strong> Tasks, journal entries, relationship notes, habits, and preferences are stored in browser storage (e.g. localStorage). Clearing site data or using a different browser profile removes or isolates that copy.</li>
      <li><strong>With Supabase (optional):</strong> If you enable sync or pair mode, selected data is stored in your Supabase project: device preferences, paired “Talk about” items, optional email-triage tasks, push subscription endpoints, and related metadata. Your project’s region and retention follow your Supabase settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> The static app may be served from GitHub Pages or another host; that host sees normal HTTPS requests (URLs, timing, IP) but not the contents of your encrypted traffic beyond what the platform logs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Subprocessors</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, realtime, and related APIs you configure.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (or your chosen static host) — delivery of HTML, JS, and CSS.</li>
      <li><strong>jsDelivr / unpkg</strong> — CDN scripts referenced from <code>index.html</code> (Supabase client, chrono-node) load from those networks when the app runs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Export &amp; deletion</h2>
    <p>You can export a JSON backup from Settings. To delete cloud-side rows, use Supabase tooling or contact whoever operates the project. We do not operate a central account system inside the app.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions about a deployment you use, contact the person or organization that gave you access to that instance and their Supabase project.</p>

